    {
      "id": "claim_2e5e039817c84c11a81346ca61eaa7dd",
      "statement": "Cache entries cannot collide across domains or configurations: LargeLanguageModelCacheMode (CHAT vs EMBEDDING) is a serialized field of every concrete key, so toJsonKey() — the hash key RedisCache addresses entries by — differs across domains and configurations even for identical model and content, while distinct configurations are additionally isolated per LocalCache file because CacheManager embeds parameters() in the cache name and file name and LocalCache keys entries within a file by the content-only localKey.",
      "evidence": [
