    {
      "id": "claim_9cf61d52c953455d901f7b0652dea0e8",
      "statement": "The exact serialized form of a cache key is its Redis address: CacheKey.toJsonKey() renders the key with a dedicated shared mapper using INDENT_OUTPUT, producing pretty-printed JSON with the fixed property order model, seed, temperature, mode, content and excluding the @JsonIgnore localKey; RedisCache stores and retrieves under that exact string (redis.hset/hget with the fields data and timestamp), so CacheKeySerializationTest pins byte-stable golden JSON (property order, escaping, whitespace) for both key types — any serialization change invalidates every existing Redis cache.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/llm/cache/CacheKey.java#L12-L31",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:34ad3f4f8c1b8eb64d35c749a34127c2dbb4e2710d23e04a38fe9535300174fa:"
        },
